hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16757","He said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from a freedman of theirs called Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, from a man among them from Khuzaa called Mukharrish or Muharrish, Sufyan was not firm upon his name and would sometimes say Muharris, and I did not hear it myself, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from al-Jirana at night and performed umra, then returned and morninged there as one overnight; and I looked at his back as if it were an ingot of silver."
